---
description: Reconcile the requested private runbook with actual Calendar evidence, current owner instructions and source attribution.
args:
  goal: string
returns: GoogleRunbookResult
---
Determine which runbook section, retained instruction and current appointment the request concerns. Compose the local evidence read, installed Calendar investigation, approval judgment, source attribution and scoped document-revision workflow to establish the requested result. Let the goal, actual evidence and dependencies determine continuation; an inspection does not authorize a write, and permission alone does not request one.

Compare current event identity and revision with the actual approved time, venue and document scope. Retained history is not present authority. Missing, stale or conflicting evidence requires an honest decision, not a neighboring event or invented approval. Preserve other passages and concurrent author changes. Use actual changed-head feedback to revisit the current evidence before deciding whether a new proposal remains authorized.

Return the supported decision, actual write readback or null, and genuine source attribution when requested or needed to resolve the question. Use null for attribution not performed; its availability does not require an unrelated investigation. Preserve the difference between a requested correction completed at a verified revision and a diagnostic or held continuation. Do not claim a scheduling change, approval or persisted revision from a semantic proposal alone.
